course: dictionary
lesson: 1489
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and caustic is one of them. The first meaning is about chemicals: something caustic can burn or eat away skin and other materials. In «lye is very caustic», the history sentence tells you that lye is dangerous to touch.
explain: The second meaning is about words and people. A caustic remark is cruel and sharp, said in a clever, sarcastic way. Nobody is burned, but the hurt can sting just as much. Use the context to choose the meaning: is the word describing a substance, or a person's comment?
explain: Look for clues around the word. Is someone pouring, mixing or washing with something? Then it means able to burn. Is someone speaking or writing a sharp, unkind comment? Then it means cruel and sarcastic. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Caustic means able to burn or eat away skin and other materials by a chemical action.
fact: «Caustic soda» is a strong chemical that can burn skin and eyes, so never touch it.
fact: Drain cleaner and oven cleaner can be caustic too: keep them locked away and read the hazard label.
fact: Caustic can also mean cruel and sharp in a clever, sarcastic way, as in «a caustic remark».
fact: In a story, a caustic comment tells the reader that a character is being bitingly unkind.
exercise: The lab sheet says «caustic soda» must be kept locked away. Why? | It smells of flowers | It is too heavy to lift | *It can burn skin and eyes | It tastes very sweet
exercise: «Her caustic remark made the whole class go quiet.» What does caustic mean here? | Bright and glowing | Very old and cracked | *Cruel and sharp, said in a clever, sarcastic way | Able to burn skin like a chemical
exercise: Which word in «lye is very caustic» tells you that lye can burn? | lye | very | is | *caustic
test: In «He gave a caustic smile and said nothing», what does caustic suggest? | Bright like a lamp | Wet and cold | Warm and loving | *Sharp and sarcastic, a bitingly unkind look
test: Oven cleaner is caustic. What should you do before using it? | Leave it open on the bench | *Read the hazard label and keep it away from children | Taste a little to check it | Mix it with juice to make it nicer
exam: In «The caustic comment hurt her feelings for days», which meaning fits best? | *Cruel and sharp, in a clever, sarcastic way | Giving out light | Able to burn skin and eat away materials | Very old
